The shop worker is directly across the counter, about arm’s length away, facing the camera wearer and extending an ice cream cone within easy reach. The counter separates them; neither person blocks the other’s path. Another person appears only in the distance outside and is walking away. No bouquet or plate is present or accessible.

The appropriate response is to accept the offered cone and thank the worker, following normal norms of politeness and gratitude.

